`public-surface.json` pins every runtime export reachable through a
`package.json` `exports` subpath. `public-surface.test.ts` fails when the two
disagree, so widening the API is a visible diff rather than a side effect of an
`export *`.

Types are not pinned: they are erased before the test can enumerate them.

Regenerate after an intentional change, from `packages/core`:

```bash
cat > src/__gen-surface.mts <<'EOF'
import { readFileSync, writeFileSync } from 'node:fs'
import { resolve } from 'node:path'
import { pathToFileURL } from 'node:url'

const pkg = JSON.parse(readFileSync('package.json', 'utf-8'))
const surface: Record<string, string[]> = {}
for (const [sub, dist] of Object.entries(pkg.exports as Record<string, string>)) {
  const src = pathToFileURL(resolve(dist.replace('./dist/', './src/'))).href
  surface[sub] = Object.keys(await import(src)).sort()
}
writeFileSync('src/public-surface.json', JSON.stringify(surface, null, 2) + '\n')
EOF
npx tsx src/__gen-surface.mts && rm src/__gen-surface.mts
```
